X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup The Rebel Craft Collective": "https://www.meetup.com/the-rebel-craft-collective/events/314772453/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_the_rebel_craft_collective
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Rebel Craft Collective
UID:event_314772453@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260616T044902Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T193000
SUMMARY:Happy Hour Crafts
DESCRIPTION:The Rebel Craft Collective\nWine + tasty snacks + your latest 
 project and a friendly group of likeminded crafters... what better way to 
 unwind? Come join us!\n\nThis is a relaxed\, drop-in-friendly event. Come 
 when you can\, leave when you must. Newcomers and occasional-comers are al
 ways welcome!\n\n**What do we mean by “crafts”?**\nWhatever “craft
 ” means to you! And whatever is portable enough to bring to a wine bar. 
 Knitting\, crochet\, and other fiber arts are most common\, but we have al
 so warmly welcomed people who sketch\, color\, embroider\, bead\, and more
 . If your craft isn’t portable\, we will happily ooh and aah over photos
  of your work-in-progress\, or chat about your plans for your next project
 .\n\n**Health & Safety**\nMasks are very welcome\, and nobody will pressur
 e you to eat or drink. If the weather is nice\, we will try to sit outside
 . If you aren’t eating/drinking during the event\, please consider order
 ing some of La Dolce Vita’s delicious food to-go\, in order to help supp
 ort our gracious\, long-time venue.\n\n**Parking**\nParking in downtown Pe
 taluma is free\, but street parking has a strictly enforced 2 hour limit u
 ntil 6pm. To park for longer\, try the nearest garage:\n\n* The Second Str
 eet Garage entrance is located on C Street between First and Second Street
 s. It's all day parking on every level and a short walk to La Dolce Vita.\
 n\n**Ages**\nIt's a wine bar\, so this event is for adult crafters (though
  you're certainly not required to drink wine!). We’re okay with babes-in
 -arms if you are\, but this is not the right setting for wee crafters who 
 are moving about on their own.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-rebel-craft-collective/events/314
 772453/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260513T184316Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260513T184316Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Petalumamuseum": "https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/opening-reception-the-fabric-of-democracy/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:petalumamuseum
X-SOURCE:Petaluma Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T200000
DTSTAMP:20260615T203409
CREATED:20260612T214231Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260612T214313Z
UID:6491-1782410400-1782417600@www.petalumamuseum.com
SUMMARY:Opening Reception: The Fabric of Democracy
DESCRIPTION:Explore how quilts have served as powerful tools for civic expression for more than two centuries. \n\n\n\n\nThursday\, June 25\,  6-8 PM\nPetaluma Historical Library & Museum\n20 4th Street (Corner of 4th & B Street)\nAdmission Free\,  Reservations Requested\nJoin the Petaluma Museum for the opening celebration of The Fabric of Democracy: Quilts and the Power of the People\, a landmark exhibition exploring how quilts have expressed civic ideals\, personal stories\, and social change throughout American history. \nPresented as part of the nation’s 250th anniversary\, the exhibition features historic and contemporary quilts that illuminate the ways individuals and communities have used textile art to advocate for justice\, build community\, preserve memory\, and imagine a better future. \nThe evening will include: \n\nFirst look at the exhibition\nRemarks from the curators\nMeet-and-greet with participating artists and lenders\nLight refreshments\nAn opportunity to participate in Common Threads: A Community Quilt Project\, a collaborative quilt inspired by the Museum’s annual July 4 Wish Wall\n\nFrom abolition and suffrage to civil rights\, environmental advocacy\, and contemporary community-based projects\, The Fabric of Democracy highlights the enduring power of quilts to tell stories\, inspire dialogue\, and connect people across generations. \nCelebrate the opening of this unique exhibition and join us in reflecting on the values\, voices\, and experiences that continue to shape our shared future. \nAbout the Exhibition\nAs the United States marks its 250th anniversary\, The Fabric of Democracy invites visitors to explore how quilts have served as powerful tools for civic expression for more than two centuries. Featuring works by artists\, collectors\, and community partners\, the exhibition examines the intersections of art\, history\, identity\, and democracy through the lens of quiltmaking.  The Exhibit will run through Sunday\, August 2. \nSpecial thanks to the City of Petaluma for supporting this exhibition and its related public programs.
URL:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/opening-reception-the-fabric-of-democracy/
LOCATION:Petaluma Historical Library & Museum\, 20 4th St\, Petaluma\, CA\, United States
CATEGORIES:Announcement,Exhibit Opening Reception
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Opening-of-Fabric-of-Democracy-Exhibit.jpg
END:VEVENT
